    "durationMs": 213348,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified against every requirement.\n\n**What I built** — NestJS 11 + TypeORM 0.3 (`@nestjs/typeorm`, the framework's idiomatic persistence layer) on PostgreSQL, reading `DATABASE_URL` from the environment:\n\n- **`POST /links`** — class-validator DTO enforces absolute http/https URL with host (`new URL` based constraint) and 4–20 char `[A-Za-z0-9_-]` codes; auto-generates 8-char codes with unique-violation retry; returns 201 `{code, url, clicks: 0}` with the URL unchanged; duplicate custom code → 409\n- **`GET /links/{code}`** / **`GET /links`** — 200 with `{code, url, clicks}`; list ordered by id (creation order) with `total`; unknown → 404\n- **`GET /r/{code}`** — atomic `UPDATE clicks = clicks + 1` then 302 with the Location header set directly (not via Express's `res.redirect`, which re-encodes URLs)\n- **422 handling** — a global exception filter maps `BadRequestException` (malformed JSON + validation) to 422 with an `error` field, while preserving 404/409\n- **Migration** — `20261121000000-CreateLinksTable` creates the `links` table with a unique index on `code`; `start.sh` compiles, runs `migration:run` (no-ops when applied), and serves on `0.0.0.0:8000` in the foreground\n\n**Testing done**: all happy paths, 10 malformed/invalid-input cases → 422, code boundaries (4 and 20 chars), duplicate → 409, byte-exact Location headers (query/fragment/uppercase scheme preserved), and a restart via `sh start.sh` confirming clicks and data survive. One environment quirk: `NODE_ENV=production` makes npm skip devDependencies, so `@types/*` live in regular dependencies — which also keeps the start.sh build working."
  }
